<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n44472" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Sisăpo</span></b> , ōnis,
			f., <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>a small town in</i> Hispania Baetica, <i>rich in
				mines of cinnabar</i>, now <i>Almaden in the
				Sierra Morena</i>, <i><span class="en">Plin. 3, 1, 3, § 14</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Cic. Phil.
				2, 19, 48</span></i>.—Hence, <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Sisăpōnensis</span></b> , e,
				adj., <i>of</i> or <i>belonging to Sisapo</i>, <i>Sisaponian</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">regio,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Plin.
					33, 7, 40, § 121</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">minarii,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">id.
					33, 7, 40, § 121</span></i>
			.</div>
